<title>USA: U.S. paper and pulp industry shaking off the slump.</title>
<headline>U.S. paper and pulp industry shaking off the slump.</headline>
<byline>Robert McNatt</byline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. paper and pulp industry is beginning to emerge from its deep cyclical trough as companies prepare to release second-quarter earnings which show a glimmer of improvement.</p>
<p>International Paper Co, the first big company in the group to post quarterly results, earned $0.20 per share on an operating basis, beating analysts expectations by a nickel.</p>
<p>It also announced a major restructuring Wednesday that boosted stock prices throughout the industry.</p>
